---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Slay the Spire 2 Co-op Boss Strategies &mdash; Boss Fight Guide"
  description="Slay the Spire 2 co-op boss strategies: how enemy scaling changes each boss fight, team tactics for every Act boss, secret boss encounters, and multiplayer-specific boss mechanics."
>
  <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-amber-400 not-prose mb-6">
      Boss Strategies: Co-op Boss Fights
    </h1>

    <p class="lead text-lg text-slate-300">
      Bosses in co-op are fundamentally different from solo. Enemy HP scales with player count,
      all players are targeted simultaneously, and team coordination determines survival.
      This guide covers how to approach every boss fight as a team.
    </p>

    <nav class="not-prose bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700 my-8" aria-label="Table of Contents">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-400 mb-3">Table of Contents</h2>
      <ol class="text-sm space-y-1 text-slate-300 list-decimal list-inside">
        <li><a href="#scaling" class="hover:text-amber-400">How Enemy Scaling Works in Co-op</a></li>
        <li><a href="#general" class="hover:text-amber-400">General Boss Tactics for Co-op</a></li>
        <li><a href="#act1" class="hover:text-amber-400">Act 1 Bosses</a></li>
        <li><a href="#act2" class="hover:text-amber-400">Act 2 Bosses</a></li>
        <li><a href="#act3" class="hover:text-amber-400">Act 3 Bosses</a></li>
        <li><a href="#secret" class="hover:text-amber-400">Secret Boss: Fake Merchant</a></li>
        <li><a href="#elites" class="hover:text-amber-400">Elite Fights in Co-op</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Scaling -->
    <section id="scaling" class="scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">1. How Enemy Scaling Works in Co-op</h2>

      <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-slate-800 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <thead class="bg-slate-700">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-amber-400">Players</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-amber-400">Enemy HP Multiplier</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-amber-400">Damage Scaling</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-semibold text-amber-400">What Changes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-700">
            <tr><td class="p-3">2</td><td class="p-3">~2.5x</td><td class="p-3">Moderate</td><td class="p-3">Enemies attack both players. Shared debuffs start to matter.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3">3</td><td class="p-3">~3.5x</td><td class="p-3">Significant</td><td class="p-3">Burst coordination becomes essential. Elites are very dangerous.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3">4</td><td class="p-3">~4.5x</td><td class="p-3">Heavy</td><td class="p-3">Every player must contribute Block and damage. One weak link wipes the team.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        Beyond raw numbers, bosses gain <strong>stronger defensive buffs</strong> in co-op.
        Shields require more hits to break, and certain boss mechanics (like The Guardian's defensive mode)
        activate more frequently when more players are present. Burst damage coordination is more important than ever.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- General Tactics -->
    <section id="general" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">2. General Boss Tactics for Co-op</h2>

      <div class="not-prose grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Debuff First, Damage Second</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">The debuffer applies Vulnerable and Weak on turn 1 while the team sets up or blocks. On turn 2, everyone attacks into the debuffed boss for maximum efficiency.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Spread Block Responsibility</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Boss AoE attacks hit <em>everyone</em>. No single tank can protect the team — every player must contribute Block. Rally and Beacon of Hope shine here.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Phase Through Big Attacks</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">When a boss telegraphs a massive attack, coordinate: everyone plays maximum Block. Intercept can redirect the weakest player's share to the tank.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Designate the Survivor</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Your tankiest character (Ironclad) should conserve HP when the team gets low. As long as one lives, everyone revives after the fight.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Burst at Thresholds</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">Many bosses change behavior at HP thresholds. Coordinate burst damage to skip dangerous phases. Necrobinder's Doom helps finish bosses before their final enrage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Don't Play Greedy</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">In co-op, one player trying to optimize damage while the team needs Block can wipe the run. Survive first, optimize second. The math of scaled bosses punishes greed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Act 1 -->
    <section id="act1" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">3. Act 1 Bosses</h2>

      <div class="not-prose space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">The Guardian</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            The Guardian's defensive mode (activates after taking a set number of hits) is more punishing in co-op
            because it can trigger from any player's attacks. <strong>Coordinate burst damage</strong> to skip the shielded phase.
            When it enters defensive mode, use the time to set up Powers and Block — don't waste attacks into the shield.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Coordinate attacks to skip shield phase</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Set up Powers during defensive mode</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Spread Block for Thorn damage</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">Hexaghost</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            Hexaghost's opening Inferno deals damage proportional to each player's current HP.
            Consider <em>intentionally</em> keeping HP low before the fight — the damage scales down significantly.
            The constant Burns added to everyone's deck demand strong card draw and exhaust mechanics.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Manage HP before fight for lower Inferno damage</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Burn removal options for entire team</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">Slime Boss</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            The split mechanic creates multiple slimes that attack <em>each player simultaneously</em>.
            AoE damage from Defect (Lightning orbs) or Silent (Corpse Explosion equivalent) is extremely valuable.
            Burst the boss to the smallest possible split HP threshold.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">AoE damage highly valued</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Burst to minimize split count</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Everyone needs Block after split</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Act 2 -->
    <section id="act2" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">4. Act 2 Bosses</h2>

      <div class="not-prose space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">Knowledge Demon</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            HP: ~380 solo / <strong>900+ in 4-player co-op</strong>. Heals ~30 HP solo / <strong>~60 HP per heal in co-op</strong>.
            Its gimmick forces penalty choices (fewer draws, damage per turn, reduced energy) that stack permanently.
            <strong class="text-amber-300">End the fight quickly</strong> — slow-scaling decks are punished severely.
            In co-op, each player gets their own penalty choice, so coordinate to pick penalties that hurt each deck the least.
            Necrobinder's Doom threshold is excellent here — it bypasses the healing.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Prioritize burst damage over scaling</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Doom and Poison bypass healing</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Each player picks least-harmful penalty</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">Bronze Automaton</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            Hyper Beam is a massive AoE that hits every player. When the boss starts glowing, <strong>everyone goes full Block</strong>.
            Steal its Stasis orbs (minions that it summons to power up) before the boss consumes them.
            The Automaton's minions also attack all players, spreading damage wide.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Full team Block on Hyper Beam turns</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Kill Stasis orbs before consumed</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">The Collector</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            Constantly summons minions that attack all players. AoE and multi-target damage are essential.
            Debuff the Collector while clearing adds — if you ignore the minions, the cumulative damage overwhelms everyone.
            Defect's Lightning orbs and Silent's multi-hit attacks shine here.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">AoE to clear minions</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Debuff boss while clearing</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Don't ignore adds — cumulative damage scales fast</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Act 3 -->
    <section id="act3" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">5. Act 3 Bosses</h2>

      <div class="not-prose space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">Time Eater</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            Forces card-play limits on the <em>entire team collectively</em> — the 12-card count is shared across all players.
            <strong>This is the biggest co-op trap.</strong> Don't play low-value cards. Coordinate so the team stays under the cap.
            High-impact expensive cards are better than cheap cycle. The time-warp effect restores its HP in co-op too.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Shared card-play cap — coordinate carefully</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Prioritize high-impact expensive cards</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Burst during vulnerable windows</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">Awakened One</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            Two-phase fight with cultists that attack all players. Phase 1: kill cultists while managing the boss.
            Phase 2: the boss buffs when you play Powers — in co-op, four players playing Powers stacks the buff <strong>four times faster</strong>.
            Be extremely selective about Powers. Regent's Star burst is perfect for skipping the dangerous second phase.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Limit Power usage — 4x faster scaling</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Clear cultists before phase transition</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Burst through phase 2 quickly</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-slate-700">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-lg mb-2">Donu &amp; Deca</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-3">
            Two bosses that buff each other. In co-op, <strong>focus fire is mandatory</strong>. Pick one (usually Donu — the buffer)
            and everyone attacks it until it's dead. Splitting damage between both prolongs the fight and lets their scaling spiral out of control.
            Debuffs apply to both, so Silent and Necrobinder can lock down both targets simultaneously.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Focus fire on Donu (buffer) first</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Debuffs work on both</span>
            <span class="bg-slate-700 text-slate-300 text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded">Team Block for double attacks</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Ascension 10 Double Boss -->
      <div class="not-prose bg-red-900/20 border border-red-700/40 rounded-lg p-4 mt-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-red-300"><strong>Ascension 10:</strong> You fight two Act 3 bosses back-to-back. The entire team must conserve resources across both fights. Don't burn all potions and exhaust cards on the first boss — plan for a marathon, not a sprint.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Secret Boss -->
    <section id="secret" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">6. Secret Boss: The Fake Merchant</h2>

      <div class="not-prose bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-5 border border-amber-600/40 mb-4">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-amber-400 text-lg mb-3">How to Trigger</h3>
        <ol class="text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1 list-decimal list-inside ml-2">
          <li>Get <strong>Foul Potions</strong> from the Potion Courier event (Act 2 or 3)</li>
          <li>Throw one at the <strong>fake merchant</strong> (he has subtly different dialogue)</li>
          <li>The real merchant only gives 100 gold for a Foul Potion — don't waste it on him</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Fight Details</h4>
          <ul class="text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1">
            <li>HP: ~165 (moderate, not heavily scaled)</li>
            <li>Attacks: 9-20 damage per hit</li>
            <li>No unique gimmicks — straightforward fight</li>
            <li>Mid-tier difficulty</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-700">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Rewards</h4>
          <ul class="text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-1">
            <li>4-6 free (lesser) Relics</li>
            <li>300 gold (split among players)</li>
            <li>Worth triggering whenever possible</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-4">In co-op, one player can carry the Foul Potion while others stock combat potions. The fight itself is manageable, and the relic/gold payoff is massive for the whole team.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Elites -->
    <section id="elites" class="scroll-mt-20 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-amber-300 mb-4 not-prose">7. Elite Fights in Co-op</h2>

      <p>
        Elites are <strong>even more rewarding</strong> in co-op than solo. Each elite drops relics for every player,
        effectively multiplying the value of elite hunting. However, they're also proportionally more dangerous.
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 mt-4">
        <div class="bg-green-900/20 border border-green-700/40 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-green-400 mb-2">Why Hunt Elites</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-green-300 space-y-1">
            <li>1 relic per player per elite — 4 relics for a 4-player team</li>
            <li>Gold for everyone</li>
            <li>Higher rare card drop chance</li>
            <li>Early elites = more relics across the whole run</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-red-900/20 border border-red-700/40 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-red-400 mb-2">When to Avoid Elites</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-red-300 space-y-1">
            <li>Teammates are below 50% HP</li>
            <li>Deck lacks Block consistency</li>
            <li>No potions available</li>
            <li>Right before the Act boss (play safe)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose bg-slate-800 rounded-lg p-4 mt-4 border border-slate-700">
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">
          <strong class="text-amber-400">Ascension 1 note:</strong> Swarming Elites (Ascension 1 modifier) makes elites spawn more often.
          This is actually <em>beneficial</em> in co-op — more elites = more relics = stronger team.
          Build your deck with elite hunting in mind at higher Ascension.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <div class="not-prose mt-12 flex justify-between items-center">
    <a href="/coop/card-synergies/" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline">&larr; Card Synergies</a>
    <a href="/coop/advanced-tips/" class="inline-block bg-amber-600 hover:bg-amber-500 text-black font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg transition-colors">
      Advanced Tips: Master Co-op &rarr;
    </a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
